    {
      "id": "UgzkHlx_gdr2q9S73_B4AaABAg",
      "author": "@kevinadams9468",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_n7417ek-18wzJI3ZENBm0JLEsWrCcksbQ7WKdHv1tzFUdXjGULqP2rM3Knc8d3lEC4qw=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "The kids living in then graveyard are in the Philippines..... There aren't many dead Cambodians with the name SANTIAGO.  I live in Cambodia and this video is just poorly done...\n\n1. Love Huts are a tradition of Non-Khmer tribes in the north and north east of the country. It is also found in the tribal areas of Laos and Vietnam. It is NOT a Cambodian custom, and these people are largely animist.... not Buddhist. That's number one for you.\n2. The garment industry is the only industry with an enforced minimum wage, around 240 a month. Yes women account for a large number of the employees, but the remainder are teenage boys who quits school to earn money...... and they make up then the 20% you maintain is left over .\n3. If a Cambodian tell you that sitting roadside and sharing food is essential to getting to know Khmer culture, it won;t be with noodles... that would be Vietnam. Cambodia certainly has noodle dishes, but it is a rice culture first and foremost.\n4. Your bargaining info is ludicrous. No-one bargains below 1000 Riel (.25 cents).... ? There is nothing that is bargained down to that tiny amount, and no vendor has a tilt wage expectation of only 25 cents. You are high or drunk. The vendors at the main market are wealthier than most, and some are millionaires.\n5. The villages of Tonle Sap near Siem Reap are not cute or rustic,. They are the result of Vietnam's Christian refugees wolfed up the Mekong to escape Communism. They are disliked ands unwanted in Cambodia. They do not have the legal right to build homes or structures on LAND. If they do, they are torn or burnt down by the authorities, so they built over the water. Yes, it is interesting, but it is NOT Cambodian . The villagers are subject to mandatory bribes by officials to be allowed to stay or work as fishermen.\n6. Currency info is wrong. You pay with whatever currency you have...mutually accepted, and change is whatever they can give you in whatever currency they have. If you pay in large US bills, you MAY get some USD back, but you cannot demand it. ATMs generally only dispense USD in 100s, which is a very hard thing to get rid ion in smaller restaurants and the market. And you show footage from the Philippines... Why? The app is not directed at using Riel, it is for both currencies, No one cares.\n7. @17:10 you simply lie.... this the Philippines...WHY???? Thmmor San was a response by villagers who were flooded out ion their homes and had no where else to go. It is not a choice. The graveyard is Chinese-Vietnamese, not ethnic Khmer. It is not a cultural thing. Why are you showing the Philippines???????\n8.At least you got the pepper right.",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-25T10:30:10Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
