    {
      "id": "UgxgDSVXQMB7u38MrV54AaABAg",
      "author": "@ChhormBorith",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/wUrKy-oagdiOfFHOHQ_U44vA7SfGFEhYmlXaKjxBzDiKcMKzhCTrcWpJEIotOXoGrWQbdIiiJZM=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "My story which I could recollected since 1975 to 1979 , I was 6 years old. My family evacuated from the city to rural. My family was on a run from execution lists due to my father military background. With Buddha blessing my family had survived the nightmare ordeal. My village always had enough food for everyone just to stay alive, but not stronger to fight back. I knew this because I walked across those corn fields and sweet potatoes and many others vegetables fields. Once moment in time I volunteered to work because they reward two scoops of rice. I was sick afterward almost die, I didn’t remember how old I was. Then a miracle came, war erupted between Khmer Rouge and the the Vietnamese soldiers. Finally, my family escaped to Cambodia-Thailand border and now we are living in the USA. Khmer people are very compassionate, traditional, and resilient.🙏🏻🙏🏻🙏🏻",
